# Annex scanning Annex.
#
# A rule pack is source code that quotes the thing it detects: the Article
# 5(1)(f) control contains a golden fixture of emotion-inference code so that
# the detector can be tested. Scanning this repository without these exclusions
# reports Annex itself as containing a prohibited practice — which it found,
# and which is why this file exists.
#
# Excluded files are still ingested, still hashed into the tree and still
# counted in the report's warnings. They simply produce no signals.

# The corpus: controls, classification rules and their golden fixtures.
packages/engine/src/packs/
packages/engine/src/classify/rules.ts
packages/engine/src/signals/catalogue.*.ts
packages/engine/src/benchmark/

# Deliberately non-conformant sample repositories used by the demo and tests.
fixtures/

# Primary-source legal research, which quotes the statute at length.
docs/research/

# Tests.
packages/engine/test/

# The product's own copy, which quotes the statute and shows example findings.
# A landing page that prints `candidateScore >= ADVANCE_THRESHOLD` as an
# illustration is not a recruitment system, and the sample catalogue that
# describes a credit-scoring fixture is not a credit-scoring system.
#
# Three files that used to be here are not any more. `classify/index.ts`,
# `cli/src/bin.ts` and `dossier/` were excluded for convenience rather than for
# a reason — they hold prose about regulated practices in comments and strings,
# and domain detectors now skip comments, so the exclusion has stopped being
# necessary. Leaving them out hollowed out the self-scan the CI gate depends on.
apps/web/src/app/page.tsx
apps/web/src/server/systems.ts
apps/web/src/server/narrative.ts

# Generated remediation templates, which are the compliant implementations
# Annex writes into other people's repositories.
packages/engine/src/packs/remediation-templates.ts
packages/engine/src/packs/doc-templates.ts

# Annex's own output, captured verbatim and compiled into the landing page.
# `hero-capture.ts` is a transcript of a scan of the HireFlow fixture — it
# contains the literal string `detectEmotion(frames, transcript)` because that
# is what the tool printed about a different repository. The self-scan read it
# back and reported Annex as containing a prohibited practice, which is the
# same read-back loop as `docs/examples/` below and is why both are here.
apps/web/src/app/hero-capture.ts

# Annex's own output, checked in as worked examples. A CycloneDX attestation
# describing a prohibited practice is a description of one, and on the next
# scan it would be read back as evidence about this repository — the same loop
# the remediation guard exists to break.
docs/examples/
docs/BENCHMARK.md

# The web app's runtime database. SQLite write-ahead log files are megabytes of
# binary that exist only on a machine where the app has been run, and are
# gitignored — but a scan reads the disk, not the index, so on a developer's
# tree they arrived as an oversize skip warning about a file that is not source.
apps/web/data/
